,"organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#pullrequestreview-5332989339","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122560","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#pullrequestreview-5332989339"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122560"}},"submitted_at":"2026-09-28T01:13:26Z","commit_id":"c3697aeb2f037072e55de047f1cdedb7c819676e"},{"id":5333007704,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPd89WA","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Overall looks good.\r\nWe approved the functionality.\r\n\r\nI have approved it, however there are some outstanding request changes comments that need to be addressed.\r\n\r\nMost importantly, there's an issue with compat breakage (see Tokage's comment chain).\r\n\r\nAlso, some debugging code is left in the PR that needs to be removed (or hidden inside #ifdef). At a minimum, `static int Dsegmentindexbeingcalculated;` should be inside the same #ifdef as the rest of the debugging code. Any commented out code should be removed.\r\n\r\nAlso, we found a minor issue where CHAIN colliders not part of the SpringBoneSimulator3D (disabled or excluded) are still showing as a chain even though they are not used. I do not consider this issue a blocker, just a minor gizmo issue we found when testing.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#pullrequestreview-5333007704","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122560","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#pullrequestreview-5333007704"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122560"}},"submitted_at":"2026-09-28T01:18:48Z","commit_id":"1ab07f100d3bcaa670fdaf02d8b7e5e4d8ffc656"},{"id":5333018886,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPd9pBg","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#pullrequestreview-5333018886","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122560","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#pullrequestreview-5333018886"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122560"}},"submitted_at":"2026-09-28T01:22:00Z","commit_id":"1ab07f100d3bcaa670fdaf02d8b7e5e4d8ffc656"},{"id":5346149697,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPqfFQQ","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Overall very well written. We approved the feature in the meeting and now that it has addressed the feedback it should be good to go.\n\nI tested it against both the test project as well as this fork of godot-vrm:\nhttps://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/interactor-test-godot-vrm-motion-checker/tree/godot47\n\nI do not have many examples of capsule-tapered capsule collisions so I can't personally check if the capsule case  is correct in all cases. However, the way the code is written is very clean: taking the closest sphere, then taking the sphere-tapered sphere collision is a smart way to simplify the collision math and should be correct, provided that function works.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#pullrequestreview-5346149697","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122560","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#pullrequestreview-5346149697"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122560"}},"submitted_at":"2026-09-29T06:54:28Z","commit_id":"03f416f365fe1a127fdb2ca3ef7532a87402ecf7"},{"id":5349415628,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPtmazA","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#pullrequestreview-5349415628","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122560","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#pullrequestreview-5349415628"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122560"}},"submitted_at":"2026-09-29T07:56:36Z","commit_id":"03f416f365fe1a127fdb2ca3ef7532a87402ecf7"},{"id":5352186896,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPwPkEA","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?u=9b90963f1b4f17720e50bbbe495fbe8c84c8bc8e&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think most of the behavior and architecture are good.\r\n\r\nIf I were to point out concerns:\r\n\r\n1. Regarding the behavior, it would be how a root of the chain detection is treated. The current implementation is unstable and behaves like a glitch, so we should consider whether it is possible to treat the chain root radius as 0, among other approaches.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/11e9276a-55c9-4d60-857f-4b394ee8702a\r\n\r\n[spring_bone_simulator_3d.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32802023/spring_bone_simulator_3d.zip)\r\n\r\n2. Regarding the ENUM naming, the opposite of INSIDE is missing, which makes it unclear what it is actually inside of. It should probably be named JOINT_INSIDE or TRAP_JOINT, or we should rename the current JOINT to SPHERE and offer options like SPHERE/TRAP_SPHERE/CHAIN.\r\n\r\n3. As for the Gizmo, as mentioned above, showing it only when a joint is selected would be helpful when adjusting other unrelated gizmos. If you want to display them all the time when chain collision is child, we'll either need to use dashed lines or lower the alpha (And when selecting a chain collision, you can increase the alpha or make it a solid line), otherwise, it will be hard to see when adjusting other type collisions.\r\n\r\n4. Code comments should be organized and formatted.\r\n\r\nI think we should address the four points raised above, but if you are in a rush to introduce this in 4.8, we could also merge it now and fix it during the beta period.\r\n\r\n","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#pullrequestreview-5352186896","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122560","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#pullrequestreview-5352186896"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122560"}},"submitted_at":"2026-09-29T12:01:03Z","commit_id":"0f13a7e659f9bce1e3bb2eeb4d07ac80427e0d5f"}]